        "name": "USN-4468-2",
        "description": "USN-4468-1 fixed a vulnerability in Bind. This update provides the corresponding update for Ubuntu 12.04 ESM and Ubuntu 14.04 ESM.  Original advisory details:   Dave Feldman, Jeff Warren, and Joel Cunningham discovered that Bind  incorrectly handled certain truncated responses to a TSIG-signed request. A  remote attacker could possibly use this issue to cause Bind to crash,  resulting in a denial of service. (CVE-2020-8622)",
        "aliases": [
          "CVE-2020-8622"
        ]
      },
